WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:01.738
(light music)

00:00:01.738 --> 00:00:02.786
- I'm Stephen Wiltshire.

00:00:02.786 --> 00:00:03.953
I do drawings.

00:00:05.333 --> 00:00:06.744
- [Narrator] Stephen is
an artist who creates

00:00:06.744 --> 00:00:09.849
incredibly intricate
drawings of cityscapes.

00:00:09.849 --> 00:00:12.264
- [Stephen] I love drawing tall buildings,

00:00:12.264 --> 00:00:15.764
tall skyscrapers, skylines, street scenes.

00:00:17.418 --> 00:00:21.585
- [Narrator] And he does
this entirely from memory.

00:00:28.001 --> 00:00:31.317
When Stephen was three, he
was diagnosed as autistic.

00:00:31.317 --> 00:00:35.484
He was completely mute and
lived entirely in his own world.

00:00:37.149 --> 00:00:39.129
Early on, Stephen's teachers noticed

00:00:39.129 --> 00:00:40.866
he loved to draw.

00:00:40.866 --> 00:00:44.819
He had found his way
to connect with others.

00:00:44.819 --> 00:00:46.787
Stephen has the ability
to look at a subject

00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:49.279
once and then draw an
accurate and detailed

00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:51.739
picture of it, including
panoramas of entire

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:54.438
cities based off just a quick look.

00:00:54.438 --> 00:00:57.555
- I go up in the helicopter
and then memorize it.

00:00:57.555 --> 00:01:00.269
And then after being on the helicopter,

00:01:00.269 --> 00:01:05.093
and then straight back at the
hotel and then start to do draw.

00:01:05.093 --> 00:01:06.500
- [Narrator] His
incredible talent launched

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.861
an artistic career that has
taken him around the world.

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:13.333
- [Stephen] Los Angeles;
Dubai; Houston, Texas;

00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:14.916
and Tokyo in Japan.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.420
- [Narrator] And that's
just to name a few.

00:01:17.420 --> 00:01:20.903
- New York's my favorite,
Empire State Building,

00:01:20.903 --> 00:01:22.857
Chrysler Building, and there are lots

00:01:22.857 --> 00:01:25.190
of yellow New York taxicabs.

00:01:26.249 --> 00:01:27.352
- [Narrator] And Stephen has no plans

00:01:27.352 --> 00:01:28.914
of stopping anytime soon.

00:01:28.914 --> 00:01:31.183
- [Stephen] If someone told
me, though, people like

00:01:31.183 --> 00:01:35.350
me drawings, I feel good,
always be happy about it.

00:01:42.132 --> 00:01:45.049
(electronic music)

